# Yatra Mesh: 6-Week Agile MVP Implementation Plan

Yatra Mesh is an intelligent corporate shared transit and mesh mobility platform built to transform enterprise employee commute into high-occupancy ($\ge 90\%$), hyper-localized, RTO-compliant contract carriage routes with proactive acoustic safety and offline mesh resilience.

This plan details the full implementation of the live working MVP prototype covering all 6 sprint phases with high-fidelity UI/UX, smooth animations, interactive maps, audio telemetry, and offline synchronization.

---

## Architecture Overview

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph Enterprise ["Enterprise & Demand Layer"]
        HR["Enterprise HR Portal"] -->|"Upload Shifts & Rosters"| API_Cluster["Clustering & Demand Engine"]
        API_Cluster -->|"Structured Output"| Gemini["Gemini 1.5 Flash Routing"]
    end

    subgraph Core ["Core Fleet & Trip Engine"]
        Gemini -->|"Clusters & Virtual Stops"| Router["Polyline & Route Synthesizer"]
        Router -->|"Manifests"| DB[("PostGIS / Schema Layer")]
        DB --> Dispatcher["Dispatcher Ops Desk"]
    end

    subgraph CommuterPortal ["Commuter & Driver Portals"]
        Commuter["Commuter Portal"] <-->|"Boarding Pass & Live ETA"| DB
        Driver["Driver HUD View"] <-->|"Manifest Checklist & GPS"| DB
    end

    subgraph EdgeSafety ["Phase 4: Proactive Edge Safety"]
        Mic["Web Audio API Telemetry"] -->|"RMS > 85 dB for 3s"| SafetyLoop["Acoustic Anomaly Detector"]
        SafetyLoop -->|"10s Check-in Modal"| Commuter
        SafetyLoop -->|"Timeout / Panic Escalation"| EmergencyHold["EMERGENCY_HOLD Event"]
        EmergencyHold -->|"Contextual Alert Packet"| Dispatcher
    end

    subgraph OfflineMesh ["Phase 5: Offline PWA & Mesh Fallback"]
        Driver <-->|"Local Cache"| IDB[("IndexedDB Manifest")]
        Commuter <-->|"Offline QR Pass"| Driver
        IDB -->|"Sync Queue on Reconnect"| DB
    end
```

